-- #1 PM Kisan 2026
UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'PM Kisan Samman Nidhi provides ₹6,000 per year to small and marginal farmers in three equal installments of ₹2,000 each. Learn how to check your beneficiary status, update your bank details, and resolve common payment issues. Over 12 crore farmers benefit from this direct income support scheme.', faqs = '[{"question":"How can I check my PM Kisan payment status?","answer":"Visit pmkisan.gov.in, click on Farmers Corner, select Beneficiary Status, and enter your Aadhaar number or account number. The status shows whether the next installment has been credited and the date of the last payment."},{"question":"What should I do if my payment is pending?","answer":"First check your status on the PM Kisan portal. Common issues include Aadhaar not linked to bank, land records not updated, or name mismatch. Contact your local agriculture officer or visit the nearest CSC center for assistance."},{"question":"How are the installments scheduled?","answer":"Three installments of ₹2,000 each are released in April, August, and December every year. The exact dates are announced by the government. The amount is directly credited to the Aadhaar-linked bank account."},{"question":"Who is not eligible for PM Kisan?","answer":"Former and current government employees, income tax payers, doctors, engineers, and farmers who own more than 2 hectares of land are not eligible. Institutional landholders are also excluded."}]' WHERE id = 1;

-- #2 Ayushman Bharat Card
UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'Ayushman Bharat PMJAY provides a health cover of ₹5 lakh per family per year for secondary and tertiary hospitalization. This step-by-step guide explains how to check your eligibility using the SECC database, download your Ayushman card, and get cashless treatment at empanelled hospitals across India.', faqs = '[{"question":"How do I check if I am eligible for Ayushman Bharat?","answer":"Visit pmjay.gov.in, click on Am I Eligible, enter your mobile number or ration card number. The system checks your name against the SECC 2011 database. You can also check by visiting the nearest empanelled hospital."},{"question":"What documents are needed for Ayushman card?","answer":"You need Aadhaar card, ration card or SECC identification number, and a recent passport-size photograph. If you are in the SECC database, you can generate the e-card immediately without any documents."},{"question":"Which treatments are covered under PMJAY?","answer":"Over 1,600 medical procedures are covered including surgery, medical treatment, and day care procedures. Pre-existing diseases are covered from day one. The scheme covers hospitalization expenses up to ₹5 lakh per family per year."},{"question":"How do I get cashless treatment?","answer":"Visit any empanelled hospital with your Ayushman card and Aadhaar. The hospital checks your eligibility, gets pre-authorization from the scheme, and provides cashless treatment. You do not need to pay anything at the hospital."}]' WHERE id = 2;

-- #3 MGNREGA 2026
UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'MGNREGA guarantees 100 days of wage employment per year to every rural household in India. This detailed guide covers how to apply for a job card, find work through your Gram Panchayat, check your attendance and wages online, and track payment status through the official MGNREGA portal.', faqs = '[{"question":"How do I apply for a MGNREGA job card?","answer":"Visit your Gram Panchayat office with Aadhaar card, bank account details, and address proof. Fill Form A for registration. The Gram Panchayat verifies and issues the job card within 15 days. You can also apply through the local BDO office."},{"question":"What is the wage rate under MGNREGA in 2026?","answer":"The MGNREGA wage rate varies by state, ranging from ₹250 to ₹350 per day depending on the state-specific rate fixed by the central government. Wages are linked to the Consumer Price Index and revised annually."},{"question":"Can I get work for more than 100 days?","answer":"The scheme guarantees 100 days per household per year. However, in notified drought-prone or natural calamity areas, the limit can be extended to 150 days. Additional work beyond 100 days is subject to availability of funds and projects."},{"question":"What is the payment timeline for MGNREGA wages?","answer":"Wages must be paid within 15 days of the work being completed or within a week after the muster roll is closed, whichever is earlier. If delayed, workers are entitled to compensation under the Payment of Wages Act."}]' WHERE id = 3;

-- #4 PM Kisan Payment
UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'Learn how to check your PM Kisan payment status online using Aadhaar, bank account, or mobile number. This guide covers the complete process for tracking installments, updating bank details, resolving failed payments, and contacting the helpline for assistance.', faqs = '[{"question":"How can I check PM Kisan payment status by Aadhaar?","answer":"Visit pmkisan.gov.in, click Farmers Corner > Beneficiary Status, select Aadhaar, enter your 12-digit Aadhaar number, and click Get Data. Your complete payment history with installment dates and amounts will be displayed."},{"question":"What if my PM Kisan payment failed?","answer":"Check the failure reason on the portal — common issues include wrong account number, Aadhaar not linked to bank, or name mismatch. Visit your bank to correct the details. After correction, the amount will be credited in the next installment cycle."},{"question":"How do I update my bank account details?","answer":"Visit your nearest CSC center or bank branch with your Aadhaar and new account details. The bank updates your account in the PFMS system. You can also update through the PM Kisan portal by logging into the Farmers Corner."},{"question":"When is the next PM Kisan installment?","answer":"Installments are typically released in April, August, and December. Specific dates are announced on the PM Kisan portal and through media. Check the PM Kisan homepage for the latest installment release notification."}]' WHERE id = 4;

-- #5 Ayushman Bharat Application
UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'Complete process to apply for Ayushman Bharat PMJAY health insurance online and offline. Check eligibility through the SECC database, download the e-card, find empanelled hospitals near you, and understand the treatment coverage of ₹5 lakh per family.', faqs = '[{"question":"How do I apply for Ayushman Bharat online?","answer":"Visit pmjay.gov.in, click on Am I Eligible, enter your details to check eligibility. If eligible, you can download the e-card directly from the portal. No separate application form is needed for beneficiaries listed in the SECC database."},{"question":"What is the income limit for Ayushman Bharat?","answer":"The scheme uses SECC 2011 deprivation criteria instead of income limits. Urban workers in 11 specified occupation categories and rural families with specific deprivations (kutcha house, no adult member, SC/ST household) are automatically eligible regardless of income."},{"question":"Can I get treatment at a private hospital?","answer":"Yes, treatment at both government and private empanelled hospitals is covered. Over 25,000 hospitals are empanelled under PMJAY. Cashless treatment is available at all empanelled hospitals — you just need to show your Ayushman card."},{"question":"Does Ayushman Bharat cover COVID-19 treatment?","answer":"Yes, COVID-19 treatment is covered under Ayushman Bharat PMJAY. The scheme covers hospitalization expenses including ICU charges, ventilator support, medications, and diagnostic tests related to COVID-19 treatment."}]' WHERE id = 5;

-- #6 MGNREGA Job Guarantee
UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'MGNREGA guarantees 100 days of employment to every rural household in India. This guide explains how to demand work, get a job card, track your work days, and ensure timely wage payment. Understand your rights under the scheme including unemployment allowance provisions.', faqs = '[{"question":"How many days of work can I demand under MGNREGA?","answer":"Every rural household is entitled to 100 days of guaranteed wage employment per year. You can demand work at any time by submitting a written application to your Gram Panchayat. Work must be provided within 15 days of your application."},{"question":"What is the unemployment allowance?","answer":"If work is not provided within 15 days of your application, you are entitled to an unemployment allowance. The allowance is 25% of the wage rate for the first 30 days and 37.5% thereafter, paid by the state government."},{"question":"How is MGNREGA wage calculated?","answer":"Wages are paid on a piece-rate basis or daily basis as per the state-level schedule of rates. The minimum wage is set by the central government and varies by state (₹250-₹350 per day in 2026). Equal wages for men and women are guaranteed."},{"question":"Can I choose the type of work?","answer":"Yes, as far as possible, work should be provided within 5 km of your residence. If work is beyond 5 km, you get an additional 10% of the wage as travel allowance. Women are entitled to crèche facilities if there are at least 5 children under 6 years."}]' WHERE id = 6;

-- #7 PM Awas Yojana 2026
UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'PM Awas Yojana (PMAY) provides financial assistance of up to ₹2.67 lakh for rural housing and interest subsidy on housing loans for urban households. This guide covers the complete application process for both PMAY-G (Rural) and PMAY-U (Urban) with eligibility criteria and document checklist.', faqs = '[{"question":"What is the subsidy amount under PMAY Urban?","answer":"PMAY Urban provides an interest subsidy of 3% to 6.5% on housing loans up to ₹25 lakh, depending on the income category: EWS (3.33% subsidy up to ₹2.67 lakh), LIG (4.33% up to ₹2.67 lakh), MIG-I (4% up to ₹2.35 lakh), MIG-II (3% up to ₹2.30 lakh)."},{"question":"Who is eligible for PMAY Gramin?","answer":"PMAY Gramin is for rural households from EWS category with annual income up to ₹3 lakh. Landless families, SC/ST households, and those living in kutcha houses are given priority. The beneficiary receives ₹1.20 lakh in plain areas and ₹1.30 lakh in hilly areas."},{"question":"How do I apply for PM Awas Yojana?","answer":"For PMAY Urban, apply through the CLSS portal or visit your nearest bank. For PMAY Gramin, apply through your Gram Panchayat or the PMAY-G portal. You need Aadhaar, income certificate, and land ownership documents."},{"question":"What is the size of house under PMAY?","answer":"Under PMAY Gramin, the minimum house size is 25 sq meters with a separate kitchen and toilet. Under PMAY Urban, the minimum house size for EWS is 30 sq meters carpet area. The beneficiary can construct a larger house using their own resources."}]' WHERE id = 7;

-- #15 PM SVANidhi
UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'PM SVANidhi scheme provides collateral-free working capital loans up to ₹50,000 to street vendors affected by the COVID-19 pandemic. Over 60 lakh vendors have benefited from this scheme since 2020. Learn about loan eligibility, digital transaction incentives, and the easy application process through the official portal.', faqs = '[{"question":"Who is eligible for PM SVANidhi loan?","answer":"All street vendors who were vending on or before March 24, 2020, are eligible. The vendor must have a certificate of vending issued by the Urban Local Body or a valid identity proof showing vending activity. Family members of deceased vendors are also eligible."},{"question":"What is the loan amount and interest rate?","answer":"The initial loan is ₹10,000 with subsequent loans of ₹20,000 and ₹50,000. Interest rate is bank-specific but the government provides a 7% interest subsidy, effectively making the loan available at very low cost to the vendor."},{"question":"How do I apply for this scheme?","answer":"Apply through the PM SVANidhi portal (pmsvanidhi.mohua.gov.in) or visit your nearest bank branch. You need a vending certificate or identification, Aadhaar card, bank account, and a mobile number. The loan is processed within 15 working days."},{"question":"What are the digital transaction incentives?","answer":"Street vendors get a cashback of ₹100 per month for up to 100 digital transactions (UPI, debit card, etc.) per month. This encourages digital payment adoption among vendors. The cashback is credited directly to the vendor''s bank account."}]' WHERE id = 15;

-- #16 Atal Pension Yojana
UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'Atal Pension Yojana (APY) guarantees a minimum monthly pension of ₹1,000 to ₹5,000 from age 60, depending on your contribution. This comprehensive guide explains the pension table based on entry age, contribution amounts, exit rules, and how to open an APY account through any bank or post office.', faqs = '[{"question":"What pension amount can I get under APY?","answer":"You can choose a monthly pension of ₹1,000, ₹2,000, ₹3,000, ₹4,000, or ₹5,000 from age 60. The pension amount depends on your contribution during the accumulation period. Higher pension options require higher monthly contributions."},{"question":"What is the entry age for APY?","answer":"Any Indian citizen between 18 to 40 years of age can join APY. The younger you join, the lower your monthly contribution. For example, a 25-year-old joining for ₹5,000 pension pays just ₹210 per month, while a 40-year-old pays ₹1,406 per month for the same pension."},{"question":"What happens if I exit APY before 60?","answer":"If you exit before age 60, your contributions plus accrued interest are returned. However, if you exit within 5 years of joining, only the contribution amount is returned without interest. Government co-contribution (if applicable) is also forfeited."},{"question":"Can I continue APY after 60?","answer":"After age 60, you start receiving the guaranteed monthly pension for life. Upon your death, your spouse receives the same pension amount. After both are deceased, the total accumulated corpus is returned to the nominee."}]' WHERE id = 16;

-- #17 Digital India
UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'Digital India is a flagship government program launched in 2015 to transform India into a digitally empowered society. This guide covers key initiatives like Aadhaar-based services, DigiLocker, UMANG app, e-Governance portals, and how citizens can access government services online from anywhere.', faqs = '[{"question":"What are the main pillars of Digital India?","answer":"Digital India has three main pillars: (1) Digital Infrastructure as a Core Utility to Every Citizen - high-speed internet, digital identity, mobile banking; (2) Governance & Services on Demand - integrated services online, real-time access; (3) Digital Empowerment of Citizens - digital literacy, universal digital resources."},{"question":"How does DigiLocker work?","answer":"DigiLocker is a cloud-based platform for issuing and verifying documents digitally. Citizens can store Aadhaar, driving license, mark sheets, and other certificates in their DigiLocker account. Issued documents are legally valid under the IT Act 2000."},{"question":"What is the UMANG app?","answer":"UMANG (Unified Mobile Application for New-Age Governance) provides access to over 1,200 government services through a single mobile app. Services include EPFO, NPS, Passport Seva, Aadhaar, Income Tax, and state government services in multiple Indian languages."},{"question":"How does Aadhaar-based e-KYC work?","answer":"Aadhaar e-KYC allows instant verification of identity using biometric authentication. It eliminates the need for physical documents and in-person verification. Banks, telecom companies, and government departments use e-KYC for paperless service delivery."}]' WHERE id = 17;

-- #18-37: Fix excerpts + FAQs (same pattern)
UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'PM Awas Yojana Urban provides interest subsidy on housing loans for EWS, LIG, MIG-I, and MIG-II categories. Depending on your income, you can get up to ₹2.67 lakh subsidy. This guide explains the CLSS application process, eligibility by income bracket, and required documents.', faqs = '[{"question":"What income categories are covered under PMAY Urban?","answer":"Four categories: EWS (income up to ₹3 lakh), LIG (₹3-6 lakh), MIG-I (₹6-12 lakh), MIG-II (₹12-18 lakh). Each category has different subsidy rates and maximum loan amounts. EWS and LIG get the highest subsidy percentage."},{"question":"What is the subsidy for MIG-I category?","answer":"MIG-I households (income ₹6-12 lakh) get a 4% interest subsidy on loans up to ₹25 lakh, resulting in a net subsidy benefit of approximately ₹2.35 lakh. The loan tenure is up to 20 years."},{"question":"Can I apply for PMAY Urban if I already own a house?","answer":"No, PMAY Urban is only for families who do not own a pucca house anywhere in India. The beneficiary family should not have availed housing assistance from any other government housing scheme."},{"question":"How do I track my PMAY Urban application?","answer":"Track your application status on the PMAY Urban portal (pmay-urban.gov.in) using your application reference number. You can also check with your bank or the local Urban Local Body where you applied."}]' WHERE id = 18;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'PM Awas Yojana Gramin (PMAY-G) provides financial assistance of ₹1.20 lakh in plain areas and ₹1.30 lakh in hilly areas for construction of pucca houses. Over 3 crore houses have been completed under this scheme. Learn about the eligibility, application process, and beneficiary selection criteria.', faqs = '[{"question":"How are beneficiaries selected for PMAY Gramin?","answer":"Beneficiaries are selected using the SECC 2011 database based on housing deprivation parameters. Priority is given to SC/ST households, households with no adult member, landless families, and those living in kutcha or dilapidated houses."},{"question":"What is the house design under PMAY Gramin?","answer":"The minimum house size is 25 sq meters with a dedicated kitchen, toilet, and living area. Beneficiaries can construct as per the standard PMAY-G design or choose their own design approved by the state government."},{"question":"Can women be the head of the household for PMAY?","answer":"Yes, PMAY Gramin mandates that the house must be registered in the name of the woman head of the family, or jointly with the male head. This ensures women have property rights in rural areas."},{"question":"What happens if the house is not completed?","answer":"The financial assistance is released in installments based on construction progress. If the house is not completed within the stipulated timeline, the remaining assistance may be released only after satisfactory completion verification by the Gram Panchayat."}]' WHERE id = 19;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'India offers numerous education scholarships and schemes for students from primary school to higher education. This article covers the top 10 education schemes including National Scholarship Portal programs, state-specific scholarships, and central schemes for SC/ST/OBC and minority students.', faqs = '[{"question":"What is the National Scholarship Portal?","answer":"The National Scholarship Portal (NSP) is a one-stop platform for over 50 central and state scholarship schemes. Students can apply online, track application status, and receive scholarship amounts directly to their bank accounts through DBT."},{"question":"What is the income limit for central scholarships?","answer":"Most central scholarships under NSP have an annual income limit of ₹2.5 lakh to ₹4.5 lakh depending on the specific scheme. Pre-matric scholarships target families with income up to ₹2 lakh, while post-matric schemes go up to ₹4.5 lakh."},{"question":"Can OBC students get scholarships?","answer":"Yes, OBC students are eligible for the Dr. Ambedkar Post-Matric Scholarship for OBC Students. The scheme covers tuition fees, maintenance allowance, and other educational expenses for students from OBC families with annual income up to ₹3 lakh."},{"question":"How do I apply for education schemes in India?","answer":"Most scholarship applications are accepted through the NSP portal (scholarships.gov.in). Some state-specific scholarships have separate portals. Applications typically open between July and October each year for the academic year."}]' WHERE id = 20;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'India has several government health insurance schemes providing coverage from ₹50,000 to ₹5 lakh per family. This comprehensive list covers Ayushman Bharat PMJAY, state-specific health schemes, CGHS for government employees, and employer-provided ESI coverage for the organized sector.', faqs = '[{"question":"Which is the largest health insurance scheme in India?","answer":"Ayushman Bharat PMJAY is the largest health insurance scheme, providing ₹5 lakh cover per family to over 10 crore poor and vulnerable families. It covers 1,600+ medical procedures across 25,000+ empanelled hospitals nationwide."},{"question":"What is the income limit for Ayushman Bharat?","answer":"Eligibility is based on SECC 2011 deprivation criteria. For rural areas: families living in kutcha houses, no adult member, SC/ST families. For urban areas: workers in 11 specified occupation categories like domestic help, sanitation workers, street vendors."},{"question":"Does ESI cover dependents?","answer":"Yes, ESI covers the employee, spouse, and up to two children. Dependent parents may also be covered in some cases. The employee contributes 0.75% of wages while the employer contributes 3.25%. ESI covers medical, maternity, and disability benefits."},{"question":"What health schemes are available for senior citizens?","answer":"Senior citizens can access Ayushman Bharat PMJAY (if eligible), CGHS (if retired central government employee), state-specific senior citizen health schemes, and the Pradhan Mantri Vaya Vandana Yojana for income support."}]' WHERE id = 21;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'Indian farmers can benefit from multiple government schemes including PM Kisan Samman Nidhi (₹6,000/year), PM Kisan Maandhan (₹3,000/month pension), Kisan Credit Card (₹3 lakh loan), PM Fasal Bima Yojana (crop insurance), and PM Kisan Urja Suraksha (solar pumps). This guide compares all agriculture schemes.', faqs = '[{"question":"How many schemes are available for farmers in India?","answer":"The central government runs over 20 major schemes for farmers including PM Kisan, PM Kisan Maandhan, Kisan Credit Card, PM Fasal Bima Yojana, PM Kisan Urja Suraksha, Soil Health Card Scheme, Paramparagat Krishi Vikas Yojana, and the National Agriculture Market (e-NAM)."},{"question":"What is the PM Fasal Bima Yojana premium?","answer":"Farmers pay a nominal premium of 2% for kharif crops, 1.5% for rabi crops, and 5% for commercial/horticultural crops. The remaining premium is subsidized by the central and state governments. The scheme covers crop loss due to natural calamities."},{"question":"How much loan can I get through KCC?","answer":"Kisan Credit Card provides short-term crop loans up to ₹3 lakh at a 4% interest rate (7% with 3% prompt repayment incentive). The loan covers cultivation expenses, post-harvest costs, and farm maintenance needs. KCC is valid for 5 years with annual review."},{"question":"What is e-NAM and how does it benefit farmers?","answer":"e-NAM (National Agriculture Market) is an online trading platform connecting 1,000+ mandis across India. Farmers can sell their produce online to buyers across states, getting better prices. There are no APMC market fees on e-NAM transactions."}]' WHERE id = 22;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'India offers multiple welfare schemes for women including Ladli Laxmi Yojana, Beti Bachao Beti Padhao, PM Ujjwala Yojana (free LPG), Sukanya Samriddhi Yojana (8.2% interest), maternity benefit schemes, and one-stop crisis centers for women in distress. This guide covers all major central and state women welfare programs.', faqs = '[{"question":"What is the Ladli Laxmi Yojana benefit?","answer":"Ladli Laxmi Yojana (Madhya Pradesh) provides ₹1,00,000 to families upon the birth of a girl child, paid in installments at different life stages - ₹6,000 at birth, ₹6,000 at class 6 enrollment, ₹6,000 at class 9, ₹6,000 at class 12, and ₹75,000 at age 21."},{"question":"What is the Pradhan Mantri Matru Vandana Yojana?","answer":"PMMVY provides ₹5,000 in three installments to pregnant women and lactating mothers for their first living child. The amount is credited directly to the beneficiary''s bank account and is meant to compensate for wage loss during pregnancy."},{"question":"What are the maternity leave benefits in India?","answer":"The Maternity Benefit Act provides 26 weeks of paid maternity leave for women working in the organized sector. The employer pays the full salary during this period. The act also prohibits dismissal of women during maternity leave."},{"question":"What are the schemes for women entrepreneurship?","answer":"Key schemes include: Mudra Yojana (loans up to ₹10 lakh), Stand Up India (₹10 lakh-₹1 crore for SC/ST women), Annapurna Scheme (₹50,000 for food business), Stree Shakti Package (0.5% interest concession on loans for women entrepreneurs), and the DICCI scheme."}]' WHERE id = 23;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'India''s social welfare schemes provide pension, food security, and financial support for vulnerable groups. Key programs include the National Social Assistance Programme (NSAP) for senior citizens, widows, and disabled persons, PM Garib Kalyan Anna Yojana for food security, and various state-specific pension schemes.', faqs = '[{"question":"What is the National Social Assistance Programme?","answer":"NSAP provides monthly pension to elderly (₹200-₹500), widows (₹300-₹500), and disabled persons (₹300-₹500) living below the poverty line. The amount varies by scheme component and has been revised periodically by the central government."},{"question":"Who can get food grains under NFSA?","answer":"The National Food Security Act provides 5 kg of food grains per person per month at subsidized rates of ₹3/kg for rice, ₹2/kg for wheat, and ₹1/kg for coarse grains. It covers 67% of the population (75% rural, 50% urban) based on SECC data."},{"question":"What is the difference between NSAP and state pension schemes?","answer":"NSAP is a central government scheme providing minimum pension amounts. Many states supplement NSAP with additional amounts — for example, Delhi gives ₹2,000/month for elderly vs NSAP''s ₹500/month. State top-ups vary significantly across states."},{"question":"How do I apply for social welfare benefits?","answer":"Apply at your local SDM office, Tehsil office, or through the state social welfare department portal. You need BPL certificate, Aadhaar, age proof, bank account, and category certificate (SC/ST/OBC if applicable). Most states now accept online applications."}]' WHERE id = 24;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'PM-KISAN is the Government of India''s flagship income support scheme providing ₹6,000 per year to small and marginal farmers. This article explains the complete eligibility criteria based on landholding, the three-installment payment schedule, the beneficiary list checking process, and how farmers can resolve common issues.', faqs = '[{"question":"What is the objective of PM Kisan?","answer":"PM Kisan Samman Nidhi aims to supplement the financial needs of small and marginal farmers in procuring agricultural inputs. The scheme provides ₹6,000 per year in three installments to help farmers meet crop expenses and improve their livelihood."},{"question":"Who is covered under PM Kisan?","answer":"All small and marginal farmers who own less than 2 hectares of cultivable land are covered. The scheme is inclusive regardless of caste, religion, or gender. Farmers from all states and union territories are eligible."},{"question":"How can I check if I am in the PM Kisan beneficiary list?","answer":"Visit pmkisan.gov.in, click on Know Your Status in the Farmers Corner section. You can search by Aadhaar number, bank account number, or mobile number. The portal shows your current verification status and payment history."},{"question":"What documents are needed for PM Kisan registration?","answer":"You need Aadhaar card, land records showing less than 2 hectares of ownership, bank account passbook with IFSC code, and a passport-size photograph. Mobile number linked to Aadhaar is required for OTP verification."}]' WHERE id = 25;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'Step-by-step guide for farmers to apply for PM Kisan Samman Nidhi online in 2026. Learn how to register on the PM Kisan portal, upload land documents, link Aadhaar with your bank account, and track your application status. Includes troubleshooting tips for common registration errors.', faqs = '[{"question":"How do I register for PM Kisan online?","answer":"Visit pmkisan.gov.in, click on New Farmer Registration under Farmers Corner. Enter your Aadhaar number, name, mobile, and land details. Upload scanned copies of land records and Aadhaar. Submit — your application goes to the local agriculture officer for verification."},{"question":"Can I apply offline for PM Kisan?","answer":"Yes, visit your nearest Common Service Centre (CSC), Patwari, or local agriculture officer. They will fill the form and upload documents on your behalf. This is helpful for farmers who are not comfortable with online portals."},{"question":"How long does PM Kisan verification take?","answer":"After online submission, the local agriculture officer or patwari verifies your land records. This typically takes 30 to 60 days. You can check the status on the PM Kisan portal. Rejected applications show the reason for rejection."},{"question":"What if my Aadhaar is not linked to bank account?","answer":"Visit your bank branch to update Aadhaar linkage with your savings account. This is mandatory for receiving PM Kisan payments. You can check Aadhaar-bank linkage status online through the NPCI mapper portal."}]' WHERE id = 26;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'Kanya Sumangala Yojana is a flagship girl child scheme of the Uttar Pradesh government providing ₹15,000 in phased benefits from birth to graduation. Eligibility criteria include family income below ₹3 lakh, UP residency, and two girl child limit. Learn the complete qualification rules and application process.', faqs = '[{"question":"What is the income limit for Kanya Sumangala?","answer":"The annual family income from all sources must not exceed ₹3 lakh. Income certificate from the competent authority is required at the time of application. The income limit was revised from ₹2 lakh to ₹3 lakh in the latest budget."},{"question":"How much benefit is provided under the scheme?","answer":"Total benefit of ₹15,000 is provided in installments: ₹5,000 at birth (or up to 1 year), ₹5,000 at Class 1 enrollment, ₹1,000 at Class 6, ₹1,000 at Class 10, ₹1,000 at Class 12, and ₹2,000 at graduation/diploma completion."},{"question":"Can I apply for Kanya Sumangala for more than 2 daughters?","answer":"No, the scheme covers a maximum of two girl children per family. This includes biological daughters and adopted daughters. Multiple births (twins) are counted as one for the two-child limit."},{"question":"What documents are needed for the application?","answer":"Birth certificate of the girl child, Aadhaar card of parents, UP domicile certificate, family income certificate below ₹3 lakh, bank account of the mother or guardian, and a recent photograph of the girl child with parents."}]' WHERE id = 27;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'Complete checklist of documents required for Ayushman Bharat PMJAY treatment. From Aadhaar card and ration card to SECC identification and hospital referral papers, this guide covers every document you need for cashless hospitalization, e-card generation, and claim settlement.', faqs = '[{"question":"What documents are mandatory for Ayushman Bharat treatment?","answer":"Mandatory documents include Ayushman Bharat e-card or beneficiary ID, Aadhaar card of the patient, and family identification from SECC database. Additional documents may include ration card, voter ID, and hospital referral letter if applicable."},{"question":"Do I need to carry physical documents to the hospital?","answer":"The Ayushman e-card (digital) is sufficient in most cases. The hospital checks your eligibility online using your beneficiary ID. However, carrying Aadhaar and a printed copy of the e-card is recommended for quick processing."},{"question":"What if I lost my Ayushman card?","answer":"You can download the e-card again from pmjay.gov.in using your mobile number or ration card number. Visit any Common Service Centre (CSC) for assistance. The card is available free of cost and can be regenerated multiple times."},{"question":"Can I add family members to my Ayushman card?","answer":"Family members are automatically included if they are part of the SECC-listed family. The cover is ₹5 lakh per family per year, shared among all family members. Newborns are automatically covered under the mother''s card."}]' WHERE id = 28;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'Ladli Behna Yojana is a Madhya Pradesh government scheme providing ₹1,000 per month (₹12,000 per year) to married women aged 21-60. Learn the complete online application process, eligibility criteria including income limit of ₹2.5 lakh, required documents, and how to check beneficiary status.', faqs = '[{"question":"Who is eligible for Ladli Behna Yojana?","answer":"Married women aged 21 to 60 years who are permanent residents of Madhya Pradesh are eligible. The annual family income should not exceed ₹2.5 lakh. Women who are income tax payers or government employees are not eligible."},{"question":"How much financial assistance is provided?","answer":"Selected beneficiaries receive ₹1,000 per month, credited directly to their bank account through DBT. The scheme benefits over 1.25 crore women across Madhya Pradesh. The amount has been increased from ₹1,000 in subsequent budgets."},{"question":"How do I apply online for Ladli Behna?","answer":"Visit the Ladli Behna portal (ladlibehna.mp.gov.in), register with your mobile number, fill the application form with personal details, upload required documents, and submit. You can also apply through the Samagra portal or visit your local Anganwadi."},{"question":"What documents are needed for the scheme?","answer":"Aadhaar card, MP domicile certificate, income certificate below ₹2.5 lakh, marriage certificate, bank account passbook in the applicant''s name, and a recent passport-size photograph. Husband''s Aadhaar and income details are also required."}]' WHERE id = 29;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'West Bengal offers several women and child welfare schemes including Kanyashree Prakalpa (₹25,000 for girl child), Rupashree Prakalpa (₹25,000 for marriage aid), Swasthya Sathi (₹5 lakh health cover), and Lakshmir Bhandar (₹500-₹1,000 monthly allowance). This guide covers all WB welfare programs with eligibility and application details.', faqs = '[{"question":"What is Kanyashree Prakalpa and its benefit?","answer":"Kanyashree Prakalpa is West Bengal''s girl child empowerment scheme providing annual scholarships of ₹500 to ₹1,000 for girls aged 13-18 and a one-time grant of ₹25,000 at age 18 if she remains unmarried and continues education. Over 1.5 crore girls have benefited."},{"question":"What is Lakshmir Bhandar scheme?","answer":"Lakshmir Bhandar provides monthly financial assistance to women in West Bengal. General category women get ₹500 per month while SC/ST women get ₹1,000 per month. The amount is directly transferred to the woman''s bank account."},{"question":"What is Rupashree Prakalpa?","answer":"Rupashree Prakalpa provides a one-time financial assistance of ₹25,000 to families for the marriage of their adult daughter. Families with annual income up to ₹3 lakh are eligible. The assistance is given at the time of the daughter''s marriage."},{"question":"How does Swasthya Sathi work?","answer":"Swasthya Sathi provides cashless health insurance coverage of ₹5 lakh per family per year to West Bengal residents. It covers both hospitalization and day-care procedures. The scheme has over 7 crore beneficiaries and 2,000+ empanelled hospitals."}]' WHERE id = 30;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'Swasthya Sathi (West Bengal) and Ayushman Bharat PMJAY (Central) both offer ₹5 lakh health coverage but differ in eligibility criteria, coverage scope, hospital networks, and application processes. This comparison guide helps you understand which scheme is better for your family based on your location and eligibility.', faqs = '[{"question":"Which scheme has wider coverage — Swasthya Sathi or Ayushman Bharat?","answer":"Ayushman Bharat has nationwide coverage with 25,000+ empanelled hospitals across India. Swasthya Sathi primarily covers West Bengal with 2,000+ hospitals. If you travel frequently outside WB, Ayushman Bharat provides better access to hospitals across states."},{"question":"Can I get benefits from both schemes?","answer":"If you are eligible for both, you can avail benefits from both schemes. However, for a single hospitalization, you can claim from only one scheme — you cannot double-claim the same medical expense. Choose the scheme that provides better coverage for your specific treatment."},{"question":"What are the income eligibility differences?","answer":"Ayushman Bharat uses SECC 2011 deprivation criteria without specific income limits. Swasthya Sathi has a family income limit of ₹5 lakh per year for general category and ₹7 lakh for SC/ST families in West Bengal, making it accessible to a wider population."},{"question":"Which scheme has better coverage for pre-existing diseases?","answer":"Both schemes cover pre-existing diseases from day one with no waiting period. Swasthya Sathi covers 1,000+ medical procedures while Ayushman Bharat covers 1,600+ procedures. Ayushman Bharat has a slightly broader procedure list."}]' WHERE id = 31;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'Bihar Student Credit Card Scheme provides education loans up to ₹4 lakh at just 4% interest rate for students from Bihar. This step-by-step guide covers the complete application process, eligibility criteria (Bihar domicile, income limit, admission requirements), the online portal, and the document checklist.', faqs = '[{"question":"What is the maximum loan amount under Bihar Student Credit Card?","answer":"Students can get an education loan of up to ₹4 lakh at just 4% per annum interest rate. For female students, the maximum loan is ₹5 lakh. The loan covers tuition fees, hostel fees, books, and other educational expenses."},{"question":"Who is eligible for the scheme?","answer":"Students must be permanent residents of Bihar, aged 18+ years, and have secured admission in a recognized course after Class 12. The annual family income should not exceed ₹3 lakh from all sources. Both boys and girls are eligible, with higher limits for girls."},{"question":"How do I apply for the Bihar Student Credit Card?","answer":"Apply online through the Bihar Student Credit Card portal (biharstudentcreditcard.com). You need to register with your mobile number, fill personal and academic details, upload documents, and select your preferred bank. Track application status on the same portal."},{"question":"What is the repayment period for the loan?","answer":"The loan repayment starts 1 year after the course completion or 6 months after getting a job, whichever is earlier. The repayment period is up to 5 years. No collateral is required for loans up to ₹4 lakh."}]' WHERE id = 32;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'PM Awas Yojana Gramin provides ₹1.20 lakh (plain) or ₹1.30 lakh (hilly) for pucca house construction to rural households. This detailed guide covers beneficiary selection through SECC data, eligibility criteria including land ownership and income limits, application process through Gram Panchayat, and installment release schedule.', faqs = '[{"question":"What is the installment schedule for PMAY Gramin?","answer":"The assistance is released in three installments: 40% at foundation level, 40% at lintel level, and 20% at completion stage. Each installment is released after verification of construction progress by the Gram Panchayat or block officer."},{"question":"Can I get a loan in addition to PMAY Gramin assistance?","answer":"Yes, beneficiaries can avail a top-up loan of up to ₹70,000 from banks for constructing a larger house. The loan is available at subsidized interest rates under the PMAY-G scheme. The total combination of subsidy and loan should suffice for a 25 sq meter house."},{"question":"What if I already have a kutcha house?","answer":"If you have a kutcha house, you are eligible for PMAY Gramin to construct a pucca house. The old kutcha house must be demolished after the new house is completed. The Gram Panchayat verifies that the beneficiary does not own a pucca house anywhere."},{"question":"Is PMAY Gramin available to landless families?","answer":"Yes, landless families are eligible. However, they need to have land allotted by the state government or have purchased land. The scheme provides assistance for house construction only — land procurement is the responsibility of the beneficiary."}]' WHERE id = 33;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'Maharashtra offers several education schemes for students including the Rajarshi Shahu Maharaj Merit Scholarship, Eklavya Scholarship for tribal students, Post-Matric Scholarships for SC/ST/OBC, and the Maharashtra State Scholarship for minority students. This guide covers eligibility, benefits, and the Mahadbt portal application process.', faqs = '[{"question":"What is the Mahadbt portal?","answer":"Mahadbt (mahadbt.maharashtra.gov.in) is the Maharashtra government''s direct benefit transfer portal for scholarships. Students can apply for over 50 education schemes through a single login. Applications are accepted annually between August and November."},{"question":"What is the Rajarshi Shahu Maharaj Merit Scholarship?","answer":"This scholarship is awarded to meritorious students from EWS families for higher education. The scholarship covers tuition fees up to ₹20,000 per year plus maintenance allowance of ₹5,000-₹10,000. Students must have secured 80%+ marks in the previous qualifying exam."},{"question":"How much scholarship do SC/ST students get in Maharashtra?","answer":"SC/ST students in Maharashtra get full tuition fee coverage plus maintenance allowance ranging from ₹3,000 per month (hostellers) to ₹1,200 per month (day scholars) under the Government of India Post-Matric Scholarship. The income limit is ₹2.5 lakh for SC and ₹2 lakh for ST."},{"question":"What is the Eklavya Scholarship for tribal students?","answer":"Ekblavya Scholarship is for tribal students from Maharashtra pursuing professional courses like engineering, medicine, and management. Selected students receive full tuition fees, hostel accommodation, and a monthly stipend of ₹5,000. The scholarship is renewable each year based on performance."}]' WHERE id = 34;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'MGNREGA provides 100 days of guaranteed employment to rural households. This guide covers the complete process of applying for work through job cards, understanding your rights under the scheme, tracking work days on the MGNREGA portal, and ensuring timely payment of wages at the notified state rate.', faqs = '[{"question":"How do I get a MGNREGA job card?","answer":"Visit your Gram Panchayat with Aadhaar and bank details. Submit Form A for household registration. The job card is issued within 15 days free of cost. Each registered household gets one job card with names of all adult family members willing to work."},{"question":"What work is provided under MGNREGA?","answer":"Work includes water conservation, drought proofing, irrigation canals, land development, rural connectivity, and sanitation projects. The work is provided within 5 km of the applicant''s residence. Works are approved by the Gram Sabha and implemented by the Gram Panchayat."},{"question":"How are MGNREGA wages calculated?","answer":"Wages are paid on a piece-rate basis based on the state schedule of rates. The minimum wage varies by state from ₹250 to ₹350 per day in 2026. Wages are calculated based on the amount of work completed, measured by the mate or gram rozgar sahayak."},{"question":"What is the unemployment allowance under MGNREGA?","answer":"If work is not provided within 15 days of application, the applicant is entitled to unemployment allowance. The state government pays this allowance — 25% of the wage rate for the first 30 days and 37.5% thereafter until work is provided."}]' WHERE id = 35;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'Sukanya Samriddhi Yojana (8.2% interest, 21-year tenure, ₹1.5 lakh max deposit) and Kanya Sumangala Yojana (₹15,000 phased benefit, income limit ₹3 lakh) are both girl child savings schemes but serve different purposes. This detailed comparison helps parents choose the right scheme for their daughter''s future financial security.', faqs = '[{"question":"Which scheme gives better returns — SSY or Kanya Sumangala?","answer":"Sukanya Samriddhi Yojana provides higher returns with 8.2% compound interest, while Kanya Sumangala provides fixed benefits of ₹15,000 phased over time. SSY is best for long-term savings (21 years), while Kanya Sumangala is better for immediate educational needs."},{"question":"Can I invest in both schemes simultaneously?","answer":"Yes, there is no restriction on availing both schemes simultaneously. SSY is a savings scheme requiring deposits from parents, while Kanya Sumangala is a state government scholarship scheme. Parents can invest in SSY and also apply for Kanya Sumangala benefits."},{"question":"What happens if I close SSY account early?","answer":"SSY cannot be closed before 21 years except in case of the girl child''s marriage (after 18) or critical illness. Early closure results in the interest rate being reduced to 2-3% less than the applicable rate. Partial withdrawal up to 50% is allowed after age 18 for education."},{"question":"Which states offer Kanya Sumangala?","answer":"Kanya Sumangala Yojana is specifically a Uttar Pradesh government scheme. Other states have similar schemes under different names: Ladli Laxmi (MP), Ladli Behna (MP), Kanyashree (West Bengal), Bhagyalakshmi (Karnataka), and Kunwar Bai (Chhattisgarh)."}]' WHERE id = 36;

UPDATE articles SET excerpt = 'Sambal Yojana provides social security to unorganised workers in Madhya Pradesh through scholarships for their children, financial assistance for girls'' marriage (₹25,000), one-time funeral aid (₹5,000), and maternity benefits (₹5,000). This guide explains how informal sector workers can register under the MP Samagra portal to avail all benefits.', faqs = '[{"question":"Who is eligible for Sambal Yojana?","answer":"Unorganised sector workers aged 18-60 years who are permanent residents of Madhya Pradesh are eligible. Workers include rickshaw pullers, domestic helpers, construction laborers, vendor workers, and agricultural laborers. Family income must be below ₹2.5 lakh per year."},{"question":"What benefits does Sambal Yojana provide?","answer":"Benefits include education scholarships (₹1,200-₹5,000 per year for children), marriage assistance of ₹25,000 for daughters, maternity benefit of ₹5,000, funeral assistance of ₹5,000, and accidental insurance coverage when added as a rider benefit."},{"question":"How do I register for Sambal Yojana?","answer":"Register through the MP Samagra portal (samagra.gov.in) or visit your nearest Jan Seva Kendra. You need Aadhaar, MP domicile, income certificate, and a letter from your employer or trade union confirming your unorganized sector worker status."},{"question":"Is Sambal Yojana only for MP residents?","answer":"Yes, Sambal Yojana is specifically for workers who are permanent residents of Madhya Pradesh. The benefit is portable within the state — if a registered worker moves within MP, they can transfer their registration to the new location."}]' WHERE id = 37;
